    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (78.03) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.41). **Gunnar Henderson** faces a favorable matchup against Schultz, and despite a slight penalty for the pitcher's hold efficiency, his park factor and batting order position make him our premier offensive engine. **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite start as well, benefiting from a soft xERA matchup against Ginn. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) provides perhaps the most explosive profile today; he draws a significant boost from a strong wind blowing out at the stadium, compounding the advantage of facing Rea in a favorable hitting environment.\n\nThe bottom of the lineup features a few tactical pivots, most notably **Andy Pages** (70.61) and **Drake Baldwin** (65.60), both of whom offer strong efficiency scores that solidify our daily floor. **Coby Mayo** (65.57) rounds out the high-confidence tier, overcoming his platoon split against the lefty Schultz thanks to a massive park factor boost. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Miguel Vargas**, who scored a respectable 48.65. While his elite xwOBA (0.407) is tantalizing, he narrowly missed the cut because the current configuration of **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** provides a more stable, higher-efficiency path toward our 5x5 targets, especially given the premium we place on the lineup order reliability of **Liam Hicks** and **Andy Pages**.\n\nWe are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses closely, specifically for **Liam Hicks**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**. Should these players shift significantly in the order, their daily efficiency scores will require re-calibration. Risks remain regarding **Nasim Nunez** (49.31); while his speed is a coveted asset for our stolen base targets, his positioning at the bottom of the order and the presence of a tough arm like Tolle limit his upside. We continue to hold **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, as his absence continues to press our depth, forcing us to lean heavily on the current active roster to maintain our pace in Roto scoring.",
